   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine rend="printed">
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_29">27, RUE CASIMIR-PÉRIER (VII<hi rend="superscript">
                                        <hi rend="underline">E</hi>
                                    </hi>)</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine rend="printed">                          	LITTRÉ 88-89</addrLine>
                            <addrLine xml:space="preserve">           	Paris <date when="1934-01-28">January the 28-th.1934</date></addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Mr Budgen</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>           	<name type="person" key="joyc82">Mr Joyce</name> wants me to write to you to say that he hopes you have received his <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="letter" key="L_71587">telegram</rs>
                        </seg> of congratulations. It is curious that <rs type="work">your book</rs> should have been put on sale on exactly the same day as the <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">American edition</rs>
                        </seg> was offered for sale.</p>
                    <p>           	The next paragraph is confidential.</p>
                    <p>           	There has been in the last few days a very hard and serious relapse in the state of health of <name type="person" key="joyc07">Miss Joyce</name> and Mr Joyce does not know what he may have to do in the course of the next days. He might have to go down to Divonne or elsewhere <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">to accompany her</seg>. In these circumstances and though he would greatly like to see you would it not be more advisable for you to postpone your journey to Paris for a little time?</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>                          	very sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="leon93">                                         	Paul Léon</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Sent from JJ to Budgen on 19 January 1934.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">The American edition of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> was published on 25 January 1934.</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">Lucia Joyce was eventually taken to the psychiatric hospital Les Rives de Prangins in Switzerland (adjacent to the town of Divonne, France).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
